WHAT WAS BUILT
  Core (poc/codec/, additively -- R0):
    ak_parse_<Root>       one per root.  Parses into the host-owned decode
                          context and makes NO reverse call.
    ak_bdr_reserve        pre-size the record buffer
    ak_bdr_footprint      what the last parse deposited
    ak_bdr_drain          copy whole records into host memory, from a cursor
    ak_bdr_ptr            the records in place, for a host with no pinning problem
    ak_bdr_reset          drop the records, keep the allocation
    ak_bdr_count_forward  counting build only; the host reports the crossings it
                          made through ak_bdr_footprint, which takes a const
                          context and cannot bump a counter itself (R5)
    ak_rt::bdr            the record buffer and its cursor
  Host (poc/rust/):
    replay_<root>         walk the records, calling the SAME apply_*/new_*/add_*
                          the push vtable registers
    parse_drain_with_*    parse, drain in chunks, replay each chunk
    parse_walk_with_*     parse, ak_bdr_ptr, replay in place
    parse_walk_opaque_*   the same with the replay's calls made opaque (R5)

  THE DIFF IS STRICTLY ADDITIVE.  `git diff --stat` over poc/codec/crates is
  2,048 insertions and ZERO deletions: every byte of the push family's emitted
  codec is unchanged, which is what R0 requires of a slice's contribution.  The
  one change to an existing type is a field appended to DecCtxImpl, which is
  opaque to every host.  Section 2 below re-runs the push family's own gate
  rather than asserting that.

